kastlevania may be new to Netflix but to  video game fans Castlevania is a 30 year  old series that's been a mainstay of  gaming since Nintendo entertainment  systems heyday while the Netflix show  isn't directly based on one game in  particular it's loosely based on  Castlevania 3 Dracula's curse released  in the u.s. in 1990 for the NES but  paying close attention to the action and  set pieces reveals the cartoon creators  actually pulled from a lot of different  games in the series if you're a 10 of  the most notable references we found  while watching the show there are  probably a few that we missed so join  the conversation and drop any references  you noticed into the comments if you  liked this video be sure to subscribe to  GameSpot and GameSpot universe for the  latest in gaming and entertainment  number one Dracula teleports with a  pillar of fire after learning that his  wife was killed for witchcraft in  episode 1 Dracula teleports from their  humble homestead back to the magical  castle via a pillar of fire this is a  technique used by Dracula and a few of  the Castlevania games most notably  during the final boss battle in super  Castlevania 4 on the Super Nintendo and  during the prologue of Playstations  Castlevania Symphony of the Night which  was a retelling of the final battle from  Castlevania Rondo of blood number 2  fountain overflowing with blood you have  to give Netflix credit for allowing the  Castlevania cartoon to feature as much  brutality and violence as it does  seriously it's incredibly gruesome  sometimes in one notable seen when  Dracula's hell spawn rise to kill the  citizens of Wallachia as punishment for  killing his wife Lesa we see a city  drenched in blood in human remains  though it may be just a coincidence a  fountain overflowing with blood can also  be seen and astute Castlevania fans may  remember seeing a similar fountain in  the fifth stage of Castlevania  bloodlines on the Sega Genesis 3 Trevor  bares a scar over his left eye Trevor  the lead character of the Netflix show  made his debut back in Castlevania 3  Dracula's curse that game made with low  res graphics and a limited color palette  made it difficult to discern Trevor's  appearance beyond the colour of his  clothes in Castlevania curse of darkness  Trevor reappears and this time we get a  better look at his facial features  including a scar across his left eye a  scar that's almost identical to  the one seen on Trevor's face in the  show for Trevor faces off with a cyclops  when Trevor fights the Cyclops to rescue  sefa during the show it's a direct  reference to a boss battle in  Castlevania 3 Dracula's curse where  Trevor fights the same creature in an  environment littered with petrified  humans five cephas masqueraded as a man  before her true identity is revealed  sefa is a female but when we first see  her in the show she's dressed in men's  garb making Trevor's revelation that  she's a woman come as a surprise you  seekers wouldn't do that  what dress the girls like boys this is  yet another callback to Castlevania 3 in  the manual for that game sefa was  referred to as he and her face was  obscured in the accompanying character  portrait but at the end of the game  Seifer removes her hood during the  closing credits and her long hair gives  away her true identity 6 trevor loses  his cape when he gets down to business  for a large portion of the 4 episode  Netflix show Trevor is seen wearing a  cape but once it's up to him to step up  against evil he purposefully sheds his  cape  hello again Castlevania 3 where Trevor  goes capless once the action begins 7  jumping across the massive gear works  when Trevor and sefa fall beneath the  streets of Wallachia they quickly end up  traversing a massive room housing big  turning gears similar gears are often  featured within Castlevania games clock  towers and once again Castlevania 3  stands out as the origin of the  tradition 8 trevor swings across  platforms using his whip shortly after  Trevor and sefa across the  aforementioned gears Trevor uses his  whip to swing from one platform to  another and this is a technique used in  a few of the Castlevania games most  notably though in super Castlevania 4  number 9  Alec arts teleportation ability looks  eerily familiar  Alucard plays a major role in the final  episode of the Netflix show during a  battle with Trevor he teleports out of  harm's way leaving a ghostly after image  behind it's not a direct copy of his  movements and Symphony of the Night but  it's in that game where he adopts the  habit of quickly shifting through space  in a similar  fashioned 10 alec cards coat is directly  modeled after his coat and symphony of  the night after Alucard test Trevor and  sefa in combat he puts on a coat that is  clearly styled after his uniform and  symphony of the night that's all the  references that we found guys if you can  find any more let us know in the  comments below as always for more games  stuff keep it locked on GameSpot and if  you guys want to check out some more  entertainment content go over to  GameSpot universe we have a giveaway  right now for an exclusive 2017  comic-con t-shirt you have to watch a  little bit of our content but I mean  it's kind of worth it
 

